## Explicit acute ó/á starters (partial) — 2026-11-03

The same exact loop supports precomposed `ó` and single-storey `á`, with a
rising acute line positioned above the circle using its size and pen width.
The browser refuses an accent that would extend outside the 3500×4500 µm
cell, leaving all previously authored glyphs unchanged. Explicit TSV export
contains 49 segments for `ó` and 50 for `á`; no native curve or anchor
primitive persists. Decomposed accent graphemes and all other vowel forms
still require independently authored strokes.

The acute guides additionally admit a signed horizontal shift (-500 to 500
µm) and a nonnegative lift (0 to 500 µm). Each is visible in the separate
SVG guide, while invalid or clipped constructions refuse without mutating
the TSV draft. Browser tests cover adjusted placement and refusal; any
accepted output remains explicit integer line segments rather than a
persistent accent attachment.

## Printed two-storey a/á browser starter (partial) — 2026-11-03

The geometric starter menu now separately selects single-storey `a` and a
printed two-storey `a`, plus their accented `á` counterparts. The printed
form reuses the same mathematically circular SVG lower bowl. Its upper story
is two smooth analytic quadratic SVG arches joined to the right stem.

Replacing the chosen exact grapheme samples the bowl into 48 segments and
